{
  "_purpose": "HTTP request bodies for the deployed intake flow, REV | Intake | WordPress to Dataverse. No real person is described here.",
  "_readMeFirst": "src/tests/data/README.md",
  "_wbsTasks": [
    "4.5"
  ],
  "_status": "BLOCKED - NOT RUNNABLE YET",
  "_whyBlocked": [
    "The trigger is an HTTP request protected by Entra authentication plus a second check on the x-rev-client-id header against the rev_IntakeAllowedClientId environment variable.",
    "rev_IntakeAllowedClientId has no value in REV-GrantApplications-DEV as at 2026-08-20, so the header check cannot pass and every request would take the 401 branch.",
    "The flow itself is also in Draft state and will not respond at all until it is turned on."
  ],
  "_howToUnblock": [
    "Set a value for rev_IntakeAllowedClientId in the DEV environment - the Entra application (client) id of the WordPress registration.",
    "Turn the flow on and copy its HTTP POST URL from the trigger.",
    "Send each body below with the x-rev-client-id header set to that same client id."
  ],
  "_note": "IN-04 is the one case that is testable the moment the flow is on, because it asserts that a WRONG client id is rejected.",
